  "title": "Open Access Days 2015 Zurich",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "ETH-Bibliothek will be giving the following talks at the Open Access Days:\n\nMonday, 7 September, 16.15, session 1: (Linked) Open Data and Cultural Heritage Nicole Graf (Image Archive): from the image agency to an open data supplier: realignment of the licensing model of ETH-Bibliothek’s Image Archive.\n\nTuesday, 8 September, 10.45 , session 5: Data Repositories and Open Access Matthias Töwe (Digital Curation): research data and open access: organisation is... part and parcel of it. Barbara Hirschmann (E-Publishing): development of standards and best practices in the field of research data publication. A glance at DataCite's work.\n\nTuesday, 8 September,14.00, session 10: News for Librarians Nadja Böller (Consortium of Swiss Academic Libraries): \"Access to everything for everyone – forever.\" How the \"Nationallizenzen\" project supports the Swiss open-access movement.\n\nFurther information on the information platform open-access.net"
    }
  ],
